<title>NEW ZEALAND: RUGBY UNION-UNBEATEN AUCKLAND WIN SUPER 12 FINAL 2.</title>
<headline>RUGBY UNION-UNBEATEN AUCKLAND WIN SUPER 12 FINAL 2.</headline>
<dateline>AUCKLAND 1997-05-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Auckland Blues beat the ACT</p>
<p>Brumbies 23-7 (halftime 10-0) in the final of the Super 12</p>
<p>rugby union competition at Eden Park on Saturday.</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Auckland - Tries: Craig Dowd, Michael Jones . Conversions:</p>
<p>Adrian Cashmore (2). Penalties: Cashmore (3).</p>
<p>ACT - Tries: Joe Roff. Conversions: Roff.</p>
</text>
